  "clues": {
    "kinetics": "About 60% is absorbed orally, and food raises bioavailability to approximately 100%. It is 93% bound to plasma proteins and is mainly cleared by CYP3A4 metabolism.",
    "substance": "A hydrochloride salt with a molecular weight of 393.4 for the active moiety. It is very slightly soluble in water.",
    "product": "Tablets in 25, 100 and 150 mg strengths, approved under an NDA.",
    "safety": "No boxed warning. Rash and diarrhea are the most common adverse reactions.",
    "indication": "Metastatic non-small cell lung cancer whose tumors have specific activating mutations, and metastatic pancreatic cancer in combination with gemcitabine.",
    "mechanism": "It reversibly inhibits the kinase activity of EGFR, preventing autophosphorylation and downstream signaling. Its binding is tighter to mutant EGFR than to the wild-type receptor."
  },
  "tell": "Cigarette smoking cuts this EGFR inhibitor's AUC by 64%, while food raises its bioavailability to about 100%.",
